### Vendor Email Response App — local HTTP flows
### Requires the VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client).
### Start the Functions host first:
###   cd src/communicator_app/src
###   func start
###
### The host accepts the architecture's `workflow-queue` envelopes on a single
### route (`POST /api/workflow-queue`). The trigger dispatches on `eventType`:
###
###   * `email.received`     — start a new workflow (1st HITL pause: operations plan approval)
###   * `approval.responded` — resume from a checkpoint
###
### The HTTP twin returns the envelopes that *would* have been published to
### `hitl-queue` in the response body so you can copy `checkpointId` between
### requests without a Service Bus emulator.
###
### Run order:
###   1. Happy path: start → approve command → approve email
###   2. Command rejection path: start → reject command → terminal completion
###   3. Email rejection path: start → approve command → reject email → terminal completion
###   4. Invalid approval path: start → invalid approvalStatus → error

@host = http://localhost:7071
@workflowInstanceId = next-communicator-08dd4a3e-5b07-4e1a-9b3f-1c6d2e8f9a01
@commandRejectWorkflowInstanceId = next-communicator-command-reject-08dd4a3e-5b07-4e1a-9b3f-1c6d2e8f9a02
@emailRejectWorkflowInstanceId = next-communicator-email-reject-08dd4a3e-5b07-4e1a-9b3f-1c6d2e8f9a03
@invalidApprovalWorkflowInstanceId = next-communicator-invalid-08dd4a3e-5b07-4e1a-9b3f-1c6d2e8f9a04

# NOTE: If you change message models (add/remove fields in workflow/messages/),
# you must delete all files in checkpoints/ before re-running. Stale checkpoints
# carry the old graph signature hash and will cause:
#   "workflow paused with pending request_info but no checkpoint was persisted"
# Alternatively, use a different workflowInstanceId to avoid collisions.
#
# NOTE: In production ENFORCE_WORKFLOW_IDEMPOTENCY=true rejects duplicate
# workflowInstanceIds. Locally it defaults to false so you can re-run the same
# ID without clearing checkpoints. If you enable it locally, change the
# @workflowInstanceId above or run `task app:checkpoints:clear` between runs.

### 1. Start workflow (email.received)
# @name start
POST {{host}}/api/workflow-queue
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queueName": "workflow-queue",
  "eventType": "email.received",
  "workflowInstanceId": "{{workflowInstanceId}}",
  "internetMessageId": "<LOGIC_APP_INTERNET_MESSAGE_ID>@vendor.example",
  "storagePrefix": "{{workflowInstanceId}}",
  "checkpointId": null,
  "receivedAt": "2026-05-07T16:49:51Z"
}

###
# Captured from the start response; first hitl-queue envelope = VMS plan approval.
@commandCheckpointId = {{start.response.body.result.hitl_messages[0].checkpointId}}

### 2. Resume — approve VMS plan (1st pause; approvalType: command)
# @name resumeCommand
POST {{host}}/api/workflow-queue
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queueName": "workflow-queue",
  "eventType": "approval.responded",
  "workflowInstanceId": "{{workflowInstanceId}}",
  "workflowPrefix": "{{workflowInstanceId}}",
  "checkpointId": "{{commandCheckpointId}}",
  "approvalType": "command",
  "approvalStatus": "approved"
}

###
# Captured from the command-approval resume; second hitl-queue envelope = draft review.
@emailCheckpointId = {{resumeCommand.response.body.result.hitl_messages[0].checkpointId}}

### 3. Resume — approve draft (2nd pause; approvalType: email) → workflow completes
POST {{host}}/api/workflow-queue
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queueName": "workflow-queue",
  "eventType": "approval.responded",
  "workflowInstanceId": "{{workflowInstanceId}}",
  "workflowPrefix": "{{workflowInstanceId}}",
  "checkpointId": "{{emailCheckpointId}}",
  "approvalType": "email",
  "approvalStatus": "approved"
}

### 4. Start workflow for command rejection path
# @name startCommandReject
POST {{host}}/api/workflow-queue
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queueName": "workflow-queue",
  "eventType": "email.received",
  "workflowInstanceId": "{{commandRejectWorkflowInstanceId}}",
  "internetMessageId": "<LOGIC_APP_INTERNET_MESSAGE_ID_COMMAND_REJECT>@vendor.example",
  "storagePrefix": "{{commandRejectWorkflowInstanceId}}",
  "checkpointId": null,
  "receivedAt": "2026-05-07T16:49:51Z"
}

###
@commandRejectCheckpointId = {{startCommandReject.response.body.result.hitl_messages[0].checkpointId}}

### 5. Resume — reject VMS plan (1st pause; expect terminal completion and no second HITL message)
POST {{host}}/api/workflow-queue
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queueName": "workflow-queue",
  "eventType": "approval.responded",
  "workflowInstanceId": "{{commandRejectWorkflowInstanceId}}",
  "workflowPrefix": "{{commandRejectWorkflowInstanceId}}",
  "checkpointId": "{{commandRejectCheckpointId}}",
  "approvalType": "command",
  "approvalStatus": "rejected"
}

### 6. Start workflow for email rejection path
# @name startEmailReject
POST {{host}}/api/workflow-queue
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queueName": "workflow-queue",
  "eventType": "email.received",
  "workflowInstanceId": "{{emailRejectWorkflowInstanceId}}",
  "internetMessageId": "<LOGIC_APP_INTERNET_MESSAGE_ID_EMAIL_REJECT>@vendor.example",
  "storagePrefix": "{{emailRejectWorkflowInstanceId}}",
  "checkpointId": null,
  "receivedAt": "2026-05-07T16:49:51Z"
}

###
@emailRejectCommandCheckpointId = {{startEmailReject.response.body.result.hitl_messages[0].checkpointId}}

### 7. Resume — approve VMS plan for email rejection path
# @name resumeEmailRejectCommandApprove
POST {{host}}/api/workflow-queue
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queueName": "workflow-queue",
  "eventType": "approval.responded",
  "workflowInstanceId": "{{emailRejectWorkflowInstanceId}}",
  "workflowPrefix": "{{emailRejectWorkflowInstanceId}}",
  "checkpointId": "{{emailRejectCommandCheckpointId}}",
  "approvalType": "command",
  "approvalStatus": "approved"
}

###
@emailRejectCheckpointId = {{resumeEmailRejectCommandApprove.response.body.result.hitl_messages[0].checkpointId}}

### 8. Resume — reject draft (2nd pause; expect terminal completion and no outbound send)
POST {{host}}/api/workflow-queue
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queueName": "workflow-queue",
  "eventType": "approval.responded",
  "workflowInstanceId": "{{emailRejectWorkflowInstanceId}}",
  "workflowPrefix": "{{emailRejectWorkflowInstanceId}}",
  "checkpointId": "{{emailRejectCheckpointId}}",
  "approvalType": "email",
  "approvalStatus": "rejected"
}

### 9. Start workflow for invalid approval input path
# @name startInvalidApproval
POST {{host}}/api/workflow-queue
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queueName": "workflow-queue",
  "eventType": "email.received",
  "workflowInstanceId": "{{invalidApprovalWorkflowInstanceId}}",
  "internetMessageId": "<LOGIC_APP_INTERNET_MESSAGE_ID_INVALID>@vendor.example",
  "storagePrefix": "{{invalidApprovalWorkflowInstanceId}}",
  "checkpointId": null,
  "receivedAt": "2026-05-07T16:49:51Z"
}

###
@invalidApprovalCheckpointId = {{startInvalidApproval.response.body.result.hitl_messages[0].checkpointId}}

### 10. Resume — invalid command approvalStatus (expect error, not business-terminal completion)
POST {{host}}/api/workflow-queue
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queueName": "workflow-queue",
  "eventType": "approval.responded",
  "workflowInstanceId": "{{invalidApprovalWorkflowInstanceId}}",
  "workflowPrefix": "{{invalidApprovalWorkflowInstanceId}}",
  "checkpointId": "{{invalidApprovalCheckpointId}}",
  "approvalType": "command",
  "approvalStatus": "maybe"
}

### 11. Idempotency check — replay a consumed checkpointId; expect status: already-resumed
POST {{host}}/api/workflow-queue
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queueName": "workflow-queue",
  "eventType": "approval.responded",
  "workflowInstanceId": "{{workflowInstanceId}}",
  "workflowPrefix": "{{workflowInstanceId}}",
  "checkpointId": "{{commandCheckpointId}}",
  "approvalType": "command",
  "approvalStatus": "approved"
}

### 12. Error case — unknown eventType (expect 400)
POST {{host}}/api/workflow-queue
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "queueName": "workflow-queue",
  "eventType": "unknown.thing",
  "workflowInstanceId": "{{workflowInstanceId}}"
}
